Pattern matching inspects choice payloads.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    event = WindowEvent::Resized(1280)

    if event is {
        case Resized(width, height) if width > 1920: io.line("wide")
        case Resized(width, height): io.line([: [width] x [height]])
        else: io.line("no size")
    }
]

Qualified patterns such as `WindowEvent::Opened` use the same lexical header rule:
no whitespace, line break or comment may appear on either side of `::`.

### Capture contract

- A payload pattern must include every declared field.
- Captures stay in declaration order.
- Each source capture name must exactly match its declared field name.
- `as local_name` renames only the arm-local binding.
- Duplicate local binding names are invalid.
- Payload captures are immutable arm-local bindings.
- An unguarded payload arm covers the complete variant. A guarded arm covers only values for which the guard succeeds.
- The guard and body see every capture, including fields the constructor filled from defaults. Other arms have their own scope.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Response = {
        Pending |
            retry_count I32 = 0,
            message String,
        |,
        Complete,
    }

    response = Response::Pending(message = "waiting")

    if response is {
        case Pending(retry_count, message as pending_message):
            io.line(pending_message)
        case Complete: io.line("done")
    }
]

Payload captures also work in inline and block single-predicate value matches:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    message = if response is Pending(retry_count, message) then message else "ok"

    message = if response is Pending(retry_count, message) {
        then message
    else
        then "ok"
    }
]

### Deferred and rejected forms

Direct payload field access is deferred:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    message = response.message
]

Payload field mutation is rejected.

Wildcard payload captures are not supported.

Named assignment is not match syntax:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    case Pending(retry_count, message = text): io.line(text)
]

Nested payload patterns and nested exhaustiveness are deferred.

See @../branching/#patterns-and-exhaustiveness (Patterns and exhaustiveness)
for match-level rules.
